{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"And they brought out an evil report of the land… to the children of Israel\"</b> — is that they went away from before Moses and Aaron, and would say in their tents that it is a land that devours its inhabitants. For at first, when they said before Moses that the land flows with milk and honey, except that the people is strong, and Caleb would say, \"For we are well able to overcome it,\" the people were wavering — some of them trusting in their own strength and might, and some of them in the help of HaShem against the mighty. Then they brought forth a report against them in private, as it is written: \"The land through which we passed…\" and so on, until they caused all the congregation to murmur. And this is the meaning of what it says (Numbers 14:36): \"And they returned, and caused all the congregation to murmur against him, to bring out an evil report of the land.\" And this was because these men, when they saw the people who were as tall as cedars, lofty and massive as oaks, their terror fell upon them and they melted the hearts of their brethren. And when they saw that the Israelites were still deliberating to go up, and Joshua and Caleb were strengthening their hearts, they brought out a false report in order to nullify their going up by all means. And know that a מוציא דבה (bringer-out of an evil report) is a fool who tells a falsehood, but one who tells the truth is called a מביא דבה (bringer of a report), as it is said: \"And Joseph brought an evil report of them to their father\" (Genesis 37:2). And for this they were punished to die in the plague, as it is said: \"And the men, who brought out an evil report of the land, died by the plague before HaShem\" (Numbers 14:37)." "<b>\"It is a land that devours its inhabitants, and all the people that we saw in it are men of stature\"</b> — A land, when it is bad and the waters are scarce and foul and the land is unproductive, does not produce men of stature; rather, its people would be poor and bloated, short of stature and lacking strength! But the report of the spies, saying that that land has a powerful climate and a heavy nature, and its waters and fruits are thick and heavy, and they produce growth to a very great degree, and the constitutions of ordinary human beings cannot bear them — only the giants and men of stature who possess strong natures by their constitution, who are massive in their height and stature — therefore it produces very large men and kills off all the rest of mankind, as is the way with coarse foods. <b>\"And there we saw the Nephilim\"</b> — the three sons of Anak, and they are <b>\"of the Nephilim\"</b>, the ancient ones about whom you have heard, that they are the mighty men who were of old, the men of renown (Genesis 6:4). And since the matter of the Nephilim of the generations of Noah was known in the world, they mentioned to them that these sons of Anak are from among them, in order to frighten and dismay them. Therefore they now said, <b>\"And we were in our own sight as grasshoppers, and so we were in their sight\"</b>:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "Ramban cites Genesis 37:2 with the same Hebrew verb root ד-ב-ה; his distinction is between the hif'il מוציא ('bringing out,' i.e. fabricating) and the general  מביא ('bringing,' i.e. reporting faithfully).", 1 "The word משכלת describing the land is uncertain in meaning; rendered here as 'unproductive' following context, though some read it as 'lacking' or 'defective.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:05:13.472181542Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}